      "text": "First, we need to convert the given base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to their base ten equivalents, perform the multiplication, and then convert the result back to base seven. Finally, we will find the sum of the digits of the resulting base seven number.\n\n1. Convert \\(24_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18\\]\n2. Convert \\(30_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21\\]\n3. Perform the multiplication in base ten:\n\\[18 \\times 21 = 378\\]\n4. Convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base seven. We do this by finding the coefficients for the powers of 7:\n\\[378 \\div 7^2 = 378 \\div 49 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 51\\]\n\\[51 \\div 7^1 = 51 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 2\\]\n\\[2 \\div 7^0 = 2 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 2\\]\nReading the coefficients from highest to lowest, we get \\(378_{10} = 772_7\\).\n\n5. The base seven number \\(772_7\\) represents the digits 7, 7, and 2. The sum of these digits is:\n\\[7 + 7 + 2 = 16\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
